# A guarded import nested inside another guarded import compiled the arm the
# program excluded.
#
# MECHANISM: PyPreScanImports -- the token walk that resolves every import
# ahead of the parse -- tracked ONE try at a time and keyed its arm-deadness
# test on `depth <= tryAt`, where `tryAt` is the DEPTH of that single try. A
# nested try left `tryAt` at the OUTER try's depth, so the test was false at
# every clause boundary of the inner one and the whole arm-deadness logic was
# skipped. The walk then resolved the dead arm like any other import.
# Measured with PXXDBG=n.impscan: `DEDENT to depth 1 tryAt=0 -> clause logic 0`.
#
# WHY IT IS A CORRECTNESS BUG AND NOT AN UNSUPPORTED SHAPE. `try: import X /
# except ImportError:` is the only conditional-compilation mechanism Python
# has, so a nested guard is nested conditional compilation and resolving the
# excluded arm is compiling code the source said not to compile.
#
# THE OBSERVABLE IS A WRONG VALUE AS READILY AS AN ERROR. The reported case
# errored only because its dead arm imported a module pxx cannot compile; where
# the dead arm is ordinary Python it resolves silently and its unit alias --
# first-wins -- answers every member read through the live arm's name.
#
# POSITIVE CONTROL, measured 2026-09-20 against stable_linux_amd64/default/
# pinned (pin v412, which predates the fix): the three-deep shape is REFUSED,
# `no member c_uint came of the qualifier ctypes` for the ctypes spelling, so
# this row cannot pass on the pre-fix compiler.
# bug-n-a-nested-import-guard-compiles-the-dead-arm
import nilpy_nestguard as g

# The program selects the INNERMOST guard's `else` arm: outer misses, middle
# misses, `math` resolves. Every other arm is dead.
#
# Read through BOTH doors, because they reach the arm skip differently: a unit
# alias (`from . import mod as impl`) is a compile-time first-wins table, and a
# symbol import (`from .mod import N as sym`) resolves through flat unit scope.
# A fix to one layer leaves the other silent, which is the history of this area.
print("selected", g.selected())
